## Interface: 120100
## Title: Mapzeroth (Rebuild) - Modern
## Notes: Rebuilt Mapzeroth engine, Modern dataset (development build, retail)
## Author: tr0tsky
## Version: 2.0.0-dev
## SavedVariables: MapzerothRebuildDB

# The `_Mainline` suffix is Blizzard's own convention for "load this one on retail" when a
# folder carries several .toc files -- so this now loads for real in the _retail_ client via
# the Mapzeroth-Rebuild junction, not just tests/harness.py (`--toc
# Mapzeroth-Rebuild_Mainline.toc`). Interface 120100 vs Mapzeroth-Rebuild.toc's 16001 (Forever)
# is what should keep the two apart even though Forever's own WOW_PROJECT_ID reads as Mainline
# too (see Constants.lua) -- unconfirmed against the live client, check both actually load the
# right one before trusting this. Not the final shipped per-ruleset TOC pair either (that will
# be Mapzeroth_Mainline.toc / Mapzeroth_Forever.toc under the eventual merged addon name -- see
# docs/DESIGN.md section 1); this is just this dev repo's own folder name doing the same trick
# early, for in-game testing before that merge happens.
#
# Same engine/UI file list as Mapzeroth-Rebuild.toc, Modern data instead of Forever's: every
# engine file already reads its data tables defensively (`addon.Edges or {}` and the like), so
# the ones Modern has no data for yet -- Trainers.lua (addon.Professions), Hearth.lua/
# FindHearthNode (no inn/POI data, so ctx.hearthNode never resolves), Relevance.lua -- should
# just come back empty rather than error (see Data/Modern/CONVERSION_NOTES.md and the
# mapzeroth-modern-port memory for what's actually missing vs. just untested this way).
# Forever-only data files (RidingSkills, Professions, WeaponSkills, PathFactors, Pois,
# Blackrock, Borders, NodeNames_enUS/TownNames_enUS/InstanceNames_enUS) are left out below on
# purpose -- Modern has no equivalents converted yet.

